---
#1814: `t.core` declares `Repo` and `Status`; `t.model` uses them in `Run`.
The suites below target units that reach them only through `t.model`, so a
suite may not write either name, but a case's view resolves both: a literal
for `Run.repo` is checked and branded as a `Repo`, `r.repo` is typed `Repo`,
and the test scaffold imports each from `t.core` so a lowered case can spell
it.
---
commons t.core

type Repo = String where NonEmpty

fn Repo.shout(self) -> String {
  "\(self)!"
}

type Status = enum { Pending, Done }
